  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Suppose $n\\in\\mathbb Z$. Write down and then prove the contrapositive of each of the following statements:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "If $3n$ is even, then $n$ is even.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $n$ is odd, then $3n$ is odd.\n\nWrite $n=2k+1$; then $3n=2(3k+1)+1$.",
          "worked": "Contrapositive: if $n$ is odd, then $3n$ is odd.\n\nLet $n=2k+1$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3n&=3(2k+1)\\\\3n&=6k+3\\\\3n&=2(3k+1)+1.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $3k+1\\in\\mathbb Z$, $3n$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If $3n+5$ is odd, then $n$ is even.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $n$ is odd, then $3n+5$ is even.\n\nWrite $n=2k+1$; then $3n+5=2(3k+4)$.",
          "worked": "Contrapositive: if $n$ is odd, then $3n+5$ is even.\n\nLet $n=2k+1$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3n+5&=3(2k+1)+5\\\\3n+5&=6k+8\\\\3n+5&=2(3k+4).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $3k+4\\in\\mathbb Z$, $3n+5$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "If $5n+2$ is odd, then $n$ is odd.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $n$ is even, then $5n+2$ is even.\n\nWrite $n=2k$; then $5n+2=2(5k+1)$.",
          "worked": "Contrapositive: if $n$ is even, then $5n+2$ is even.\n\nLet $n=2k$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}5n+2&=5(2k)+2\\\\5n+2&=10k+2\\\\5n+2&=2(5k+1).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $5k+1\\in\\mathbb Z$, $5n+2$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "If $n^2-6n+5$ is even, then $n$ is odd.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $n$ is even, then $n^2-6n+5$ is odd.\n\nWrite $n=2k$; then $n^2-6n+5=2(2k^2-6k+2)+1$.",
          "worked": "Contrapositive: if $n$ is even, then $n^2-6n+5$ is odd.\n\nLet $n=2k$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}n^2-6n+5&=(2k)^2-6(2k)+5\\\\n^2-6n+5&=4k^2-12k+5\\\\n^2-6n+5&=2(2k^2-6k+2)+1.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $2k^2-6k+2\\in\\mathbb Z$, $n^2-6n+5$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "If $n^2+2n+3$ is odd, then $n$ is even.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $n$ is odd, then $n^2+2n+3$ is even.\n\nWrite $n=2k+1$; then $n^2+2n+3=2(2k^2+4k+3)$.",
          "worked": "Contrapositive: if $n$ is odd, then $n^2+2n+3$ is even.\n\nLet $n=2k+1$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}n^2+2n+3&=(2k+1)^2+2(2k+1)+3\\\\n^2+2n+3&=4k^2+4k+1+4k+2+3\\\\n^2+2n+3&=4k^2+8k+6\\\\n^2+2n+3&=2(2k^2+4k+3).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $2k^2+4k+3\\in\\mathbb Z$, $n^2+2n+3$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "If $n^2$ is odd, then $n$ is odd.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $n$ is even, then $n^2$ is even.\n\nWrite $n=2k$; then $n^2=2(2k^2)$.",
          "worked": "Contrapositive: if $n$ is even, then $n^2$ is even.\n\nLet $n=2k$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}n^2&=(2k)^2\\\\n^2&=4k^2\\\\n^2&=2(2k^2).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $2k^2\\in\\mathbb Z$, $n^2$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "If $n^2$ is not divisible by 4, then $n$ is odd.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $n$ is even, then $n^2$ is divisible by 4.\n\nWrite $n=2k$; then $n^2=4k^2$.",
          "worked": "Contrapositive: if $n$ is even, then $n^2$ is divisible by 4.\n\nLet $n=2k$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}n^2&=(2k)^2\\\\n^2&=4k^2.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $k^2\\in\\mathbb Z$, $n^2$ is divisible by 4. This also includes $n=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "If $n^2$ is even, then $n$ is even.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $n$ is odd, then $n^2$ is odd.\n\nWrite $n=2k+1$; then $n^2=2(2k^2+2k)+1$.",
          "worked": "Contrapositive: if $n$ is odd, then $n^2$ is odd.\n\nLet $n=2k+1$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}n^2&=(2k+1)^2\\\\n^2&=4k^2+4k+1\\\\n^2&=2(2k^2+2k)+1.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $2k^2+2k\\in\\mathbb Z$, $n^2$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
